Writer: paragraphs without fill share one set of fill attributes.

When the layout formats a paragraph, SwTextNode::getSdrAllFillAttributesHelper creates and keeps an
SdrAllFillAttributesHelper for it, about 0.4 KB with its shared_ptr, even when the paragraph has no fill, which is
almost every paragraph. A 2 MB DOCX with 94,000 paragraphs held 39 MB of them after its layout. For a paragraph
with no fill style, no slide background fill and no enabled float transparency the helper always holds the
default fill and the default gradient, so HstSharedNoFillAttributes (new hstnofillattributes.cxx) returns one
shared helper for all of them. A paragraph with a fill still gets its own, and an attribute change still drops the
cached helper (SwTextNode::TriggerNodeUpdate, SwClientNotify) as before.

Hook: sw/source/core/txtnode/ndtxt.cxx (2 lines), sw/Library_sw.mk; logic in sw/source/core/inc/hstnofillattributes.hxx,
sw/source/core/txtnode/hstnofillattributes.cxx.
Test: CppunitTest_sw_core_txtnode testHstNoFillParagraphsShareFillAttributes.
